= Epistemics =

'''How do we know what we claim to know? This question is not academic ornament. It is operational necessity.'''

BITwiki treats the conditions of knowing as part of the knowledge object. Evidence, source, confidence, provenance, uncertainty, review, disagreement, and lifecycle are related, but they are not the same thing.

== Human-centered epistemics ==

The strongest V1 revisions moved away from rigid gatekeeping and false numerical precision toward a human-centered model:

'''Knowledge serves human understanding, not the reverse.'''

The purpose of epistemic metadata is not to dictate belief. It is to make enough of a claim's standing visible that a reader or agent can inspect the evidence, limitations, lineage, and disagreement and reach an appropriately calibrated judgment.

A weakly supported idea can still be worth preserving as a knowledge artifact. A well-established claim can still be revised. Conflict and scrutiny are not necessarily failures; they can expose assumptions and create new knowledge.

